Important Viva Questions and Answers
Q1. What is an API?

API stands for Application Programming Interface. It allows two applications to communicate with each other.

Q2. Which API is used in this practical?

OpenWeatherMap API.

Q3. What is the use of Requests library?

It is used to send HTTP requests and fetch data from web APIs.

Q4. What is a GET request?

A GET request is used to retrieve data from a server.

Q5. What is JSON?

JSON stands for JavaScript Object Notation. It is a lightweight format used to exchange data.

Q6. What does status code 200 mean?

It means the API request was successful.

Q7. What is an API key?

An API key is a unique code used to authenticate and access an API.

Q8. What is the use of resample()?

It groups time-based data into intervals such as daily, weekly or monthly.

Q9. What is a heatmap?

A heatmap is a graphical representation of data using different colours to show values.

Q10. What is correlation?

Correlation measures the relationship between two numerical variables.

Q11. What is the difference between a line graph and a bar graph?

A line graph shows trends over time, whereas a bar graph compares different values.

Q12. What is latitude and longitude?

Latitude and longitude are geographical coordinates used to identify a location on Earth.

Q13. What is the use of units=metric?

It converts temperature into Celsius and wind speed into metres per second.

Q14. What is the use of annot=True?

It displays numerical values inside the heatmap.

Q15. What is the difference between mean(), max() and min()?
- mean() – Calculates average.
- max() – Finds the highest value.
- min() – Finds the lowest value.
